      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47511",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/eb/eb3d67406c59a2efc92a25da63a31183c5046b7b7e5c589ab0c5bcc6326aef60.png)\n\nThe Venn diagram shown above represents two events $M$ and $R$ and the probabilities of each event. $M$ represents the event that a visitor to an online music store is a fan of popular music, and $R$ represents the event that a visitor is a fan of rock music. Find the probability that a randomly selected visitor to the store who likes popular music also likes rock music.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
